# Minimal multi-sector-point mesh: an open 3-triangle fan around the center
# vertex O whose per-corner normal values read A | B | A, so the point (O, A)
# has corners in two seam-separated sectors of one position fan. (An exactly
# flat-shaded A|B|A fan cannot exist geometrically, since equal normals
# through a shared vertex force one plane; the normals here are stored values,
# as in real-world source data.)
#
#        r3 ---- O ---- r1
#           F2  /|  F0    \
#          (A) / | (B) F1  \ r0
#             /  r2  (mid)  \
#
# Faces (consistent winding):
#   F0 = (O, r0, r1)  normal A
#   F1 = (O, r1, r2)  normal B
#   F2 = (O, r2, r3)  normal A
v 0.0 0.0 0.0
v 1.0 -1.0 0.0
v 1.0 0.0 0.0
v 0.0 1.0 0.0
v -1.0 0.0 0.0
vn 0.0 0.0 1.0
vn 0.0 1.0 0.0
f 1//1 2//1 3//1
f 1//2 3//2 4//2
f 1//1 4//1 5//1
